[ISSUE #2]
Hardcoded WebSocket URL In Project - WebSocket Echo

Description:
WebSocket Echo used a hardcoded localhost URL, preventing
the application from connecting correctly when accessed
through a private IP or from another device.

Cause:
The WebSocket client was explicitly connecting to
ws://localhost:8000/ws instead of the host serving the page.

Fix:
Replaced the hardcoded URL with a dynamic WebSocket URL
using window.location.host.

Result:
The WebSocket connection now automatically uses the host
and port from the current page, allowing the application
to work across devices on the same network.